[
    {
        "content": "<p>xia-chao opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14625\">PR #14625</a> from <code>xia-chao:fix/wasi-http-expire-dropped-request</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>p3 had a TODO for a dropped receiver, so wired up <code>poll_canceled</code>. p2 can't use it, its sync guest blocks the event loop.<br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 630467551,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1791561507
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>xia-chao requested <a href=\"https://github.com/rvolosatovs\">rvolosatovs</a> for a review on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14625\">PR #14625</a>.</p>",
        "id": 630467565,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1791561511
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>xia-chao requested <a href=\"https://github.com/orgs/bytecodealliance/teams/wasmtime-wasi-reviewers\">wasmtime-wasi-reviewers</a> for a review on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14625\">PR #14625</a>.</p>",
        "id": 630467566,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1791561511
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>xia-chao updated <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14625\">PR #14625</a>.</p>",
        "id": 630470162,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1791562106
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> rvolosatovs submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14625#pullrequestreview-5519129657\">PR review</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Thanks!</p>\n<p>I think we could simplify this by dropping the guard and instead relying on <code>oneshot::Sender</code> functionality directly, what do you think?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 631701204,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1791994494
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> rvolosatovs created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14625#discussion_r4271804861\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Shouldn't this also wake the worker?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 631701206,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1791994495
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> rvolosatovs created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14625#discussion_r4271758387\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>in p3 the worker might be processing multiple requests concurrently, returning here would tear down the worker and abort processing requests that are currently in-process and prevent it from accepting more requests, I don't think that's desirable.</p>\n<p>I think we should only return here on P2 (which we can do if we always leave the vector empty on P3)</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 631701207,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1791994495
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> rvolosatovs created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14625#discussion_r4271819706\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>We probably don't want this to grow without a bound</p>\n<p>We should probably also check <code>abandoned</code> here early, since a client could have disconnected while the request was in the queue</p>\n<p>Additionally, we should probably check if this is P2 (perhaps by checking <code>&amp;prepared</code>?) and only push then</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 631701209,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1791994495
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> rvolosatovs created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14625#discussion_r4272663351\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>It seems that we could achieve the same in p2 with:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">tx</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lock</span><span class=\"p\">().</span><span class=\"n\">unwrap</span><span class=\"p\">().</span><span class=\"n\">as_mut</span><span class=\"p\">().</span><span class=\"n\">is_some_and</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">|</span><span class=\"n\">tx</span><span class=\"o\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tx</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">poll_canceled</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">cx</span><span class=\"p\">).</span><span class=\"n\">is_ready</span><span class=\"p\">())</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>If we stored clones of the <code>Arc&lt;Mutex&lt;Option&lt;Sender&gt;&gt;&gt;</code> instead of the atomic bool</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 631701210,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1791994495
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> rvolosatovs created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14625#discussion_r4271918415\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>It looks like there is a race condition here if <code>handle</code> future is dropped after the response is received, but before it's polled. Perhaps the simplest fix here could be storing the channel itself in the guard and doing <code>close</code> and <code>try_recv</code> on <code>Drop</code>?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 631701211,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1791994495
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> rvolosatovs created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14625#discussion_r4271982107\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Do we actually need the <code>abandoned</code>? Couldn't we use <code>tx</code> and <a href=\"https://docs.rs/futures/latest/futures/channel/oneshot/struct.Sender.html#method.poll_canceled\">https://docs.rs/futures/latest/futures/channel/oneshot/struct.Sender.html#method.poll_canceled</a> to check if the receiver has been dropped?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 631701212,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1791994495
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> rvolosatovs created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14625#discussion_r4273306133\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"suggestion\"><pre><span></span><code>                let closed = pin!(future::poll_fn(|cx| tx.poll_canceled(cx)));\n</code></pre></div><br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 631701214,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1791994495
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> rvolosatovs created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14625#discussion_r4272722400\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"suggestion\"><pre><span></span><code>                    handle,\n                    futures::future::select(closed, expiration)\n                )\n                .await\n                {\n                    Either::Left((result, ..)) =&gt; (result, true),\n                    Either::Right(_) =&gt; {\n                        // TODO: We should also send a cancel request to the expired\n                        // task to give it a chance to shut down gracefully, but as of\n                        // this writing Wasmtime does not yet provide an API for doing\n                        // that.  See issue #11833.  Instead, we let it continue running\n                        // as a background task until it either returns a response\n                        // (which we'll ignore) or the instance itself has expired.\n                        (Err(ExpirationError.into()), false)\n                    }\n</code></pre></div><br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 631701216,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1791994495
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> rvolosatovs created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14625#discussion_r4272728924\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>nit; could we <code>use</code> the <code>poll_fn</code> and <code>future::</code> imports here?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 631701217,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1791994495
    },
